#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/supported-releases.rst:101
#: f6b08f1aab8f42aca06dcab6bd332b9c
msgid "Note on dom0 and EOL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/supported-releases.rst:104
#: c66dc21ac0e347f6a8a1042dd61e7b2e
msgid ""
"Dom0 is isolated from domUs. DomUs can access only a few interfaces, such as "
"Xen, device backends (in the dom0 kernel and in other VMs, such as the "
"NetVM), and Qubes tools (gui-daemon, qrexec-daemon, etc.). These components "
"are :doc:`security-critical </developer/system/security-critical-code>`, and "
"we provide updates for all of them (when necessary), regardless of the "
"support status of the base distribution. For this reason, we consider it "
"safe to continue using a given base distribution in dom0 even after it has "
"reached end-of-life (EOL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/supported-releases.rst:107
#: e7bbd8110f1843918ea83981f800d6aa
msgid "Templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/supported-releases.rst:110
#: 7b9d3bb11af94eefbfcf8c16850ad789
msgid ""
"The following table shows select :doc:`template </user/templates/templates>` "
"(and :doc:`standalone </user/advanced-topics/standalones-and-hvms>`) "
"releases that are currently supported. Currently, only :doc:`Fedora </user/"
"templates/fedora/fedora>` and :doc:`Debian </user/templates/debian/debian>` "
"templates are officially supported by the Qubes OS Project. `Whonix <https://"
"www.whonix.org/wiki/Qubes>`__ templates are supported by our partner, the "
"`Whonix Project <https://www.whonix.org/>`__. Qubes support for each "
"template ends when that upstream release reaches end-of-life (EOL), even if "
"that release is included in the table below. Please see below for "
"distribution-specific notes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/downloading-installing-upgrading/supported-releases.rst:112
#: d74876251f3c4aa29901b2b9938b3a7d
msgid ""
"It is the responsibility of each distribution to clearly notify its users in "
"advance of its own EOL dates, and it is users’ responsibility to heed these "
"notices by upgrading to supported releases. As a courtesy to Qubes users, we "
"attempt to pass along upstream EOL notices we receive for select "
"distributions, but our ability to do this reliably is dependent on the "
"upstream distribution’s practices. For example, if a distribution provides a "
"mailing list similar to :ref:`qubes-announce <introduction/support:qubes-"
"announce>`, which allows us to receive only very important, infrequent "
"messages, including EOL announcements, we are much more likely to be able to "
"pass along EOL notices to Qubes users reliably. Qubes users can always check "
"the EOL status of an upstream release on the upstream distribution’s website "
"(see `Fedora EOL <https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/End_of_life>`__ and `Debian "
"Releases <https://wiki.debian.org/DebianReleases>`__)."
msgstr ""

